 if  you want to place your colors in the  same order as you found them however you  set up your your set of colors or  whatever set of hues that you decided to  use you want to be able to make sure  that they flow properly so placing them  in order will not only prevent any  confusion that could happen but it could  also help you prepare it so that your  colors would lay out properly it just  really depends on your preference so  after you add your extra blocks in you  want to make sure that the gray one  isn't covered you want to make sure that  the original white isn't covered even  though if you covered it with a white it  wouldn't matter it will still show up as  white if you want to get rid of white  all together it changes to a totally  different color that's fine as well then  you want to  pick a layer you'll see here that i  actually click layer 2 to start off but  don't pay attention to that somehow  somewhere there's an extra layer in  there so just ignore that when you place  your layers you want to make sure that  they're all in order  and you want to open that layer up  [Music]  and then you just start choosing your  colors use the color picker and just  scroll through it through the hues and  pick whatever colors you want you can  use the swatches if you want to if you  have any hex numbers in mind you can use  those something that i would recommend  if you want a little bit of variety and  you want some more color or you just  want to work with a certain range of  colors like on the spectrum i really  recommend going to this website it's  called work with color and weber color  is pretty cool because it basically lays  out the entire color spectrum like right  at your fingertips they have a color  picker wheel  they have a list where you can go by  color names like literally any other  color that you can think of you can even  make your own colors if you want to  using the color mixer feature i really  like this website and i just found it  randomly 